{% set cur = r.settings.currency %}
{% set a = r.audit %}
{% set model = r.model or "resolution" %}
{% set noun = ITEM_NOUNS[model] %}
{% set per_resolution = model == "resolution" %}
{% set ns = namespace(n=0) %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Dispute pack · {{ r.program.name or "AI bill" }} · {{ r.period.start }} to {{ r.period.end }}</title>
<style>
{% include "_style.css.j2" %}
.sign td { height: 2.6rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Bill reconciliation · {{ MODELS[model] | lower }}</div>
    <h1>{{ r.program.vendor or r.program.name or "AI bill" }}</h1>
    <div class="meta">Billing period {{ r.period.start }} to {{ r.period.end }}{% if r.program.tool %} · {{ r.program.tool }}{% endif %} · {{ r.billed.count | num(0) }} billed {{ noun }}{% if r.billed.amount is not none %} · {{ r.billed.amount | money(cur) }} billed{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="grade word" title="Amount disputed">
    <div><b>{% if r.disputed.amount is not none %}{{ r.disputed.amount | money(cur) }}{% else %}{{ r.disputed.count | num(0) }}{% endif %}</b><small>Disputed</small></div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Billed</div><div class="v">{{ r.billed.count | num(0) }}</div><div class="s">{{ noun }}{% if r.billed.amount is not none %} · {{ r.billed.amount | money(cur) }}{% endif %}</div></div>
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Billing errors</div><div class="v">{{ r.disputed.billing_errors | num(0) }}</div><div class="s">{{ r.disputed.billing_error_share | pct(1) }} of billed items{% if r.disputed.billing_error_amount %} · {{ r.disputed.billing_error_amount | money(cur) }}{% endif %}</div></div>
  {% if per_resolution and r.settings.contractual %}
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Did not hold (contract definition)</div><div class="v">{{ (r.reasons | selectattr("code", "equalto", "did_not_hold") | map(attribute="count") | first) or 0 }}</div><div class="s">repeat ticket within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days</div></div>
  {% elif a and a.negotiation %}
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Negotiation figure</div><div class="v">{{ a.negotiation.estimate | money(cur) }}</div><div class="s">range {{ a.negotiation.ci_low | money(cur) }} to {{ a.negotiation.ci_high | money(cur) }}, from the resolution audit</div></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.per_held %}
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Cost per resolution that held</div><div class="v">{{ r.per_held.estimate | unit_price(cur) }}</div><div class="s">range {{ r.per_held.ci_low | unit_price(cur) }} to {{ r.per_held.ci_high | unit_price(cur) }}</div></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if per_resolution %}
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Held</div><div class="v">{{ r.held.held | num(0) }}</div><div class="s">of {{ r.held.checked | num(0) }} checked{% if r.held.too_recent %} · {{ r.held.too_recent | num(0) }} too recent{% endif %}</div></div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<p class="headline">{{ r.headline }}</p>

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{% if per_resolution %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>The definition used</h2>
<p><b>{{ r.settings.definition_name }}:</b> a conversation the AI resolved, inside the billing period, after which the same person did not open a ticket {% if r.settings.match == "same_type" %}about the same type of issue {% endif %}within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days.</p>
{% if r.settings.contractual %}
<p class="callout info">The contract uses this definition, so every billed item that did not meet it is disputed below.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="callout warn">No contract definition was applied, so only billing errors are disputed line by line. Items that came back are counted, and the resolution audit's comparison with your agents' resolutions gives a negotiation figure. To dispute them line by line, put the definition in the contract (docs/outcome-terms.md).</p>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>How this bill is counted</h2>
{% if model == "conversation" %}
<p>Every conversation the AI took part in is billed{% if r.settings.billable %} when its outcome is one of: {{ r.settings.billable }}{% else %}, whatever its outcome: resolved, handed to a person or abandoned{% endif %}. Each billed item is matched to your own conversation log, and each conversation is followed into your ticket system to see what it delivered.</p>
{% else %}
<p>One person's conversations within {{ r.settings.session_hours | num(0) }} hours of their first count as one session{% if r.settings.billable %}, when the outcome is one of: {{ r.settings.billable }}{% endif %}. {% if r.settings.item_level %}Each billed item is matched to your conversation log, and a second item billed for the same person inside one session is disputed.{% else %}Each day's billed sessions are compared with the sessions in your own conversation log.{% endif %}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if r.settings.included %}<p class="meta">The plan includes {{ r.settings.included | num(0) }} {{ noun }} a month; amounts count only what is charged beyond that.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Reconciliation</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Reason</th><th class="n">Items</th><th class="n">Amount</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for x in r.reasons %}<tr><td>{{ x.reason }}</td><td class="n">{{ x.count | num(0) }}</td><td class="n">{{ x.amount | money(cur) }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="3">No billing errors found.</td></tr>{% endfor %}
<tr><td><b>Disputed</b></td><td class="n"><b>{{ r.disputed.count | num(0) }}</b></td><td class="n"><b>{{ r.disputed.amount | money(cur) }}</b></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
{% if per_resolution and not r.settings.contractual and r.held.came_back %}<p class="meta">{{ r.held.came_back | num(0) }} billed resolutions were followed by a repeat ticket within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days. Not disputed line by line without a contract definition.</p>{% endif %}

{% if r.paid_for %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>What the money bought</h2>
<p>{% if r.settings.item_level %}The {{ noun }} on the bill that match your records{% else %}Your records' {{ noun }} for the period{% endif %}, by what happened next. "Came back" means the same person opened a ticket {% if r.settings.match == "same_type" %}about the same type of issue {% endif %}within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Outcome</th><th class="n">{{ noun | capitalize }}</th><th class="n">Share</th>{% if r.settings.item_level and r.billed.amount is not none %}<th class="n">Billed</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for x in r.paid_for %}<tr><td>{{ x.label }}</td><td class="n">{{ x.count | num(0) }}</td><td class="n">{{ x.share | pct(1) }}</td>{% if r.settings.item_level and r.billed.amount is not none %}<td class="n">{{ x.amount | money(cur) }}</td>{% endif %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
{% if not per_resolution %}<p class="meta">Per-{{ model }} pricing charges for these whatever happened. They are not billing errors; they are why the cost of each resolution that held is higher than the price of one {{ model }}.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.lines %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Disputed items</h2>
<p class="meta">The first {{ [r.lines | length, 50] | min }} of {{ r.lines | length | num(0) }}. The full list is in <span class="mono">disputed-items.csv</span>, ready to send to the vendor. It contains the vendor's own item IDs only: no names and no ticket contents.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th class="n">Line</th><th>Item</th><th>Billed</th><th class="n">Amount</th><th>Reason</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for x in r.lines[:50] %}<tr><td class="n">{{ x.line or "" }}</td><td class="mono">{{ x.item_id or "" }}</td><td style="white-space:nowrap">{{ (x.billed_at or "")[:10] }}</td><td class="n">{{ x.amount | unit_price(cur) }}</td><td>{{ x.reason }}</td><td>{{ x.detail }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}

{% if a %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Compared with your agents' resolutions</h2>
<p>Across the period's {{ a.checked | num(0) }} checkable claims, {{ a.ai_rate | pct(1) }} came back within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days after the AI, against {{ a.baseline_rate | pct(1) }} after your agents' resolutions{% if a.standardized %} of the same types{% endif %}. Share that did not hold beyond that normal rate: <b>{{ a.failed_share.estimate | pct(1) }}</b> (range {{ a.failed_share.ci_low | pct(1) }} to {{ a.failed_share.ci_high | pct(1) }}). Audit confidence: {{ a.confidence }}.</p>
{% if r.per_held %}<p>About <b>{{ r.per_held.held | num(0) }}</b> of the period's {{ r.per_held.claims | num(0) }} claimed resolutions held (range {{ r.per_held.held_low | num(0) }} to {{ r.per_held.held_high | num(0) }}). The bill comes to <b>{{ r.per_held.estimate | unit_price(cur) }} per resolution that held</b> (range {{ r.per_held.ci_low | unit_price(cur) }} to {{ r.per_held.ci_high | unit_price(cur) }}): the number to compare across vendors and billing models.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if per_resolution %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>In the vendor's favour</h2>
<p>{{ r.unbilled.resolved_not_billed | num(0) }} conversations your records show as resolved in this period are not on the bill. They are reported so the reconciliation is fair to both sides.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if r.notes %}{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Notes</h2><ul>{% for n in r.notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Sign-off</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="sign">
<thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Name</th><th>Date</th></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr><td>Prepared by</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Reviewed by (buyer)</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Acknowledged by (vendor)</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody>
</table></div>

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
<h2><span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Data lineage</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>File</th><th class="n">Rows</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for fl in r.lineage.files %}<tr><td>{{ fl.path.split("/")[-1] }}</td><td class="n">{{ fl.rows | num(0) }}</td><td class="mono">{{ fl.sha256[:16] }}…</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Probative Labs {{ r.lineage.code.probative }} · settings <span class="mono">{{ r.lineage.settings_sha256[:12] }}</span> · run {{ r.lineage.run_at }}. Anyone with the same files can rerun this reconciliation and get the same result.</p>
<footer>Generated by Probative Labs, independent verification of what AI delivers. Method: docs/reconciliation.md and docs/billing-models.md.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
